      "title": "When to use/avoid Bucket Sort",
      "lectureOrder": 226,
      "videoOrder": 224,
      "sourceHash": "cbe39619c491f2b153c3c2ed020ccceb152152d1c19d483e88339225a7661d10",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 5.24,
          "end": 9.05,
          "en": "Now here again, the question is when we can use the bucket sort algorithm.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 9.08,
          "end": 14.42,
          "en": "Now bucket sort algorithm can be used when the input is uniformly distributed over the range.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 14.45,
          "end": 15.35,
          "en": "Now what does it mean?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 15.35,
          "end": 19.25,
          "en": "It means that we should not have various differences between the elements of the array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 19.25,
          "end": 25.22,
          "en": "If we look at this array over here, we see that the difference between these elements is not too much.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 25.22,
          "end": 27.92,
          "en": "So this means that this is uniformly distributed array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 27.95,
          "end": 31.49,
          "en": "Now if we look at this one you see that this is not uniformly distributed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 31.49,
          "end": 35.54,
          "en": "Because here the difference between 4 and 9 to one is more.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 35.57,
          "end": 38.45,
          "en": "That's why this is not a uniformly distributed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 38.45,
          "end": 42.35,
          "en": "So in this case if it is not uniformly distributed we need to avoid it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 42.35,
          "end": 45.23,
          "en": "So in this case the bucket sort will not work properly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 45.23,
          "end": 51.2,
          "en": "And when the space complexity is a concern in this case we cannot use the bucket sort because bucket",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 51.23,
          "end": 53.57,
          "en": "sort algorithm takes o n space complexity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 53.57,
          "end": 55.91,
          "en": "So hopefully everything is clear.",
          "zh": ""
        }
